          <change when="2024-03-16T11:45:18-04:00" who="http://papyri.info/editor/users/simoeis">Submit - I have emended the end of line 20. The ed.pr. had ἀφω . . . , while I read ἀφῶμε̣ν̣ (aor. subj. of ἀφίημι). It seems clear from the photo that mu followed omega--the mu resembles that in the last line (a curiosity in itself).  Epsilon and nu are a bit squished and smudged, so I underdot them, though this is not entirely necessary. καὶ ἔπεμψά σοι τὸν φαμελιάριν εἵνα μὴ ἀφῶμε̣ν̣ τὸ πραισείδιν, "And I sent you the familiaris so that we not give up (or 'surrender') the praesidium."</change>
